    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "وَعَنْهُ عَنْ عَلِيِّ بْنِ النُّعْمَانِ عَنِ ابْنِ مُسْكَانَ عَنْ إِسْحَاقَ بْنِ عَمَّارٍ عَنْ عَنبَسَةَ بْنِ مُصْعَبٍ قَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And from him, from Ali ibn al-Nu'man, from Ibn Muskhan, from Isḥāq ibn ʿAmmār, from ʿAnbasah ibn Muṣʿab, who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ جَارِيَةٌ لِي زَنَتْ أَبِيعُ وَلَدَهَا قَالَ «نَعَمْ» قُلْتُ أَحُجُّ بِثَمَنِهِ قَالَ «نَعَمْ»",
      "translations": {
        "en": "I said to Abū ʿAbdillāh (peace be upon him): A slave-girl of mine committed fornication; should I sell her child? He said: 'Yes.' I said: Should I perform Ḥajj with its price? He said: 'Yes.'"
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "The Imam (peace be upon him) rules that if a female slave commits fornication, her master may sell her child (the offspring) and use the proceeds to perform Ḥajj on his own behalf.",
      "seo_question": "What is the ruling on selling the child of a slave-girl who committed fornication and using the money for Hajj?",
      "key_terms": {
        "جَارِيَةٌ": "female slave",
        "زَنَتْ": "committed fornication",
        "وَلَدَهَا": "her child/offspring",
        "أَبِيعُ": "should I sell",
        "أ sell (I sell)"
